---
layout: base.njk
title: qrr.app – share files via QR code, no login needed
description: Send files up to 80 MB, links and text between your phone and computer. No login or install – just scan a QR code or enter a 6-digit code.
priority: "1.00"
changefreq: daily
faq:
  - q: Do I need an account or an app?
    a: No. qrr.app works in the browser on any device. You can optionally install it as an app (PWA) – on Android it then appears in the "Share" menu.
  - q: How do I send a file from my phone to my computer?
    a: On the computer, click "New session". On the phone, scan the QR code, or go to qrr.app, choose "I have a code!" and enter the 6-digit code. Pick a file and send it – download it on the computer with one click.
  - q: What is the file size limit?
    a: You can send files up to 80 MB in total per session. Texts and links are sent in the same session.
  - q: Are my files stored anywhere?
    a: No. Files are kept only in the server's memory for the duration of the session and are never written to disk. When all devices disconnect, the session and its contents disappear.
  - q: Do photos lose quality?
    a: No. The original file is sent without compression, so photos and videos keep their full quality.
  - q: Does it work between iPhone, Android, Windows and Mac?
    a: Yes. All you need is a modern browser – qrr.app works across any systems, without cables or Bluetooth.
---

